    "result_text": "All 26 tests pass, including the customer-code tests (Cp09, Cp14, Cp16). The build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI changed the `customerCode` format from `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` to `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` with a per-city sequence.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 the sole place the code is generated:\n- `generateCustomerCode` now takes `city` as well as `lastName`. It prefixes with `CITY3` (upper-cased first three letters of the city) and computes `NNNN` as a **per-city** sequence \u2014 one more than the number of existing owners whose city matches (compared case-insensitively via the existing `normalizeForComparison`), instead of the old global owner count.\n- Updated the call site to pass `owner.getCity()`.\n\n**Membership number** \u2014 no code change needed: `generateMembershipNumber` already builds `<customerCode>-M<YY>` from `owner.getCustomerCode()`, so it automatically rebuilds on the new city-prefixed code. I only refreshed the stale comment/example.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` descriptions and examples (`SYD-SMI-0007`, `SYD-SMI-0007-M26`) to match.\n\nVerification of test expectations:\n- Cp16: `customerCode` matches `[A-Z]{3}-[A-Z]{3}-\\d{4}` \u2713\n- Cp09: two owners in \"Sydney\" \u2192 `SYD-ALP-0001` / `SYD-BRA-0002`, consecutive per-city sequence \u2713\n- Cp14: `membershipNumber == customerCode + \"-M\" + YY` \u2713\n\nThe DB column widths (`customer_code VARCHAR(20)`, `membership_number VARCHAR(30)`) comfortably accommodate the longer values.",
